  "id": "binocular-perception",
  "term": "binocular perception",
  "definition": "Binocular perception is visual perception using both eyes to judge depth or distance in the third dimension. In this historical source, it is described as depending mainly on the differences between the two eyes’ images and on eye movements involved in convergence and accommodation, with other visual cues playing a secondary role.",
